# SFT execution status v0.80

2026-09-13. The approved local-only test-fixture portability correction is
complete. No new commit, push, CI retry, network, GPU or real model/data access
occurred. Gate 5 remains incomplete; native qualification has not passed.

## Correction and regression evidence

Only `tests/test_sft_import_qualification_acquisition_v1.py` changed among tracked
files. The shared acquisition fixture now lets `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory`
choose the platform's default parent and still resolves the resulting path.
Production acquisition, exact retirement `/tmp` namespace, ownership/mode
checks, workflow and native guards are unchanged.

Two new regression tests were added before correcting the setup. Both failed
against the old hardcoded parent, then passed after the one-line correction:

- All seven existing acquisition cases run with the macOS-specific parent
  simulated as unavailable, and all generated fixture directories are removed.
- A generated alternate default parent is honored and cleaned up, preventing
  replacement with another fixed path.

The exact six qualification-preflight modules pass on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7
and 3.14.6: 135 distinct top-level tests per interpreter, zero failures, errors
or skips. The two regressions additionally run eight existing cases internally;
those are not new distinct tests. Audit hooks rejected socket/process-start
operations; no such calls were attempted and no ML modules were loaded.
Ruff and git diff checks pass. The full repository suite was not rerun.

